To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: aspell / php-mysql
Message-Id: <20040609060349.GA4532 () static ! protection ! cx>
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=108681675713664

On Wed, Jun 09, 2004 at 04:51:30AM +0100, Sevan / Venture37 wrote:
> hi
> Im trying to get the php-mysql extension installed, unfortunatly there is 
> no package available for the alpha platform thus Im having to resort to 
> build the extension from src. I have managed to install the php core from 
> packages with success.
> I start the make process & it see's that I have a missing dependency for 
> the extensions which is all not available as package (aspell) & it starts 
> trying to build that, at this point it chokes & dies?!!!!
> any ideas on how I can either get aspell installed on OpenBSD 3.5 Alpha so 
> I can continue compiling the extension or where I could get hold of the 
> php-mysql extension precompiled??

try:

$ cd /usr/ports/www/php4/extensions
$ env FLAVOR="no_x11 no_bz2 no_curl no_dba no_dbase no_dbx no_domxml
no_filepro no_gd no_gmp no_imap no_ldap no_mcrypt no_mhash
no_ncurses no_odbc no_pdf no_pgsql no_shmop no_snmp no_pspell
no_sybase_ct no_xmlrpc no_xslt" make package

This will only build the mysql extension.

Typically, if there is no package available on the ftp site, it
means it didn't build for the bulk package builder, in which case
it may take some effort to get it to compile and function, either on
your part, or on the maintainer's part.

